1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,083
Good morning.

2
00:00:01,083 --> 00:00:05,995
I'm very pleased to have this opportunity to say a little about two exciting

3
00:00:05,995 --> 00:00:07,869
new developments in the city:

4
00:00:07,869 --> 00:00:12,740
the Brackenside Open-Air Swimming Pool and the children's Adventure Playground in Central Park.

5
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:18,153
As many of you may know, the idea for these initiatives came from you-The

6
00:00:18,153 --> 00:00:23,180
public, in the extensive consultation exercise which the City Council conducted last year.

7
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:28,640
And they have been realised using money from the SWRDC - the South West

8
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:29,900
Regional Development Commission.

9
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:31,537
First of all, Brackenside Pool.

10
00:00:31,537 --> 00:00:36,121
As many of the older members of the audience will remember, there used to

11
00:00:36,121 --> 00:00:40,051
be a wonderful open-air pool on the sea front 30 years ago

12
00:00:40,051 --> 00:00:43,980
but it had to close when it was judged to be unsafe.

13
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:48,765
For the design of this new heated pool, we were very happy to secure

14
00:00:48,765 --> 00:00:51,499
the talents of internationally renowned architect Ellen Wendon,

15
00:00:51,499 --> 00:00:54,575
who has managed to combine a charming 1930s design,

16
00:00:54,575 --> 00:00:59,360
which fits in so well with many of the other buildings in the area,

17
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:03,885
with up-to-the-minute features such as a recycling system - the only one of its

18
00:01:03,885 --> 00:01:08,410
kind in the world - which enables seawater to be used in the pool.

19
00:01:08,410 --> 00:01:12,590
Now, there has been quite a bit of discussion in the local press about

20
00:01:12,590 --> 00:01:16,771
whether there would be enough room for the number of visitors we are hoping

21
00:01:16,771 --> 00:01:17,368
to attract,

22
00:01:17,368 --> 00:01:21,250
but the design is deceptive and there have been rigorous checks about capacity.

23
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:27,463
Also, just in case you were wondering, we're on schedule for a June 15th opening date

24
00:01:27,463 --> 00:01:29,017
and well within budget:

25
00:01:29,017 --> 00:01:32,900
a testimony to the excellent work of local contractors Hickman's.

26
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:37,880
We hope that as many people as possible will be there on June 15th.

27
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:42,268
We have engaged award-winning actress Coral White to declare the pool open

28
00:01:42,268 --> 00:01:46,290
and there'll be drinks and snacks available at the pool side.

29
00:01:46,290 --> 00:01:51,763
There'll also be a competition for the public to decide on the sculpture we

30
00:01:51,763 --> 00:01:54,108
plan to have at the entrance:

31
00:01:54,108 --> 00:01:59,190
you will decide which famous historical figure from the city we should have.

32
00:01:59,190 --> 00:02:02,433
And now, moving on to the Central Park Playground,

33
00:02:02,433 --> 00:02:07,118
which we're pleased to announce has just won the Douglas Award for safety:

34
00:02:07,118 --> 00:02:09,640
the news came through only last week.

35
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:14,955
The unique design is based on the concept of the Global Village, with the

36
00:02:14,955 --> 00:02:19,891
playground being divided into six areas showing different parts of the world - each

37
00:02:19,891 --> 00:02:21,410
with a representative feature.

38
00:02:21,410 --> 00:02:24,257
For example, there is a section on Asia,

39
00:02:24,257 --> 00:02:29,595
and this is represented by rides and equipment in the shape of snakes, orang-utans, tigers

40
00:02:29,595 --> 00:02:33,510
and so on - fauna native to the forests of the region.

41
00:02:33,510 --> 00:02:38,472
Moving south to the Antarctic 一 we couldn't run to an ice rink l'm afraid

42
00:02:38,472 --> 00:02:42,370
but opted instead for climbing blocks in the shape of mountains.

43
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:45,480
I thought they could have had slides for the glaciers

44
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:48,590
but the designers did want to avoid being too literal!

45
00:02:48,590 --> 00:02:53,314
Then on to South America - and here the theme is El Dorado -

46
00:02:53,314 --> 00:02:57,250
games replicating the search for mines full of precious stones.

47
00:02:57,250 --> 00:03:05,048
And then moving up to North America, here there was considerable debate - I know the contribution of cinema

48
00:03:05,048 --> 00:03:09,814
and jazz was considered but the designers finally opted for rockets

49
00:03:09,814 --> 00:03:11,980
and the International Space Station.

50
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:13,782
Eastwards to Europe then,

51
00:03:13,782 --> 00:03:18,287
and perhaps the most traditional choice of all the areas:

52
00:03:18,287 --> 00:03:20,540
medieval castles and other fortifications.

53
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:21,326
Then last,

54
00:03:21,326 --> 00:03:26,830
but not least, moving south to Africa and a whole set of wonderful mosaics

55
00:03:26,830 --> 00:03:31,940
and trails to represent the great rivers of this fascinating and varied continent.

56
00:03:31,940 --> 00:03:37,260
Now, the opening date for our Global Playground is 10th July.

57
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:41,079
And again we'd love to see you there - so make a date

58
00:03:41,079 --> 00:03:45,534
and come and see this magnificent, original new amenity right in the heart of

59
00:03:45,534 --> 00:03:46,170
the city.
